#. type: Content of: <sect1><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:8 blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:12
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring the Java environment"
msgstr "Configurando o ambiente Java"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:15
#, xml-text
msgid "Setting up the environment"
msgstr "Configurando o ambiente"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:18
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"After the package installation is complete, the next step is to make sure "
"that the system can properly find the files.  If you set up your login "
"scripts as recommended in <xref linkend='postlfs-config-profile'/>, update "
"the environment by creating the <filename>openjdk.sh</filename> script, as "
"the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Depois que a instalação do pacote estiver completa, a próxima etapa é a de "
"garantir que o sistema consiga encontrar os arquivos corretamente. Se você "
"configurar teus &quot;scripts&quot; de login conforme recomendado em "
"&quot;<xref linkend='postlfs-config-profile'/>&quot;, [então] atualize o "
"ambiente criando o &quot;script&quot; "
"&quot;<filename>openjdk.sh</filename>&quot;, como o(a) usuário(a) "
"&quot;<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:25
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/openjdk.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/profile.d/openjdk.sh\n"
"\n"
"# Set JAVA_HOME directory\n"
"JAVA_HOME=/opt/jdk\n"
"\n"
"# Adjust PATH\n"
"pathappend $JAVA_HOME/bin\n"
"\n"
"# Auto Java CLASSPATH: Copy jar files to, or create symlinks in, the\n"
"# /usr/share/java directory.\n"
"\n"
"AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR=/usr/share/java\n"
"\n"
"pathprepend . CLASSPATH\n"
"\n"
"for dir in `find ${AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR} -type d 2>/dev/null`; do\n"
"    pathappend $dir CLASSPATH\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"for jar in `find ${AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR} -name \"*.jar\" 2>/dev/null`; do\n"
"    pathappend $jar CLASSPATH\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"export JAVA_HOME\n"
"\n"
"# By default, Java creates several files in a directory named\n"
"# /tmp/hsperfdata_[username]. This directory contains files that are used for\n"
"# performance monitoring and profiling, but aren't normally needed on a BLFS\n"
"# system. This environment variable disables that feature.\n"
"_JAVA_OPTIONS=\"-XX:-UsePerfData\"\n"
"\n"
"export _JAVA_OPTIONS\n"
"\n"
"unset AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR dir jar _JAVA_OPTIONS\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/profile.d/openjdk.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/openjdk.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/profile.d/openjdk.sh\n"
"\n"
"# Set JAVA_HOME directory\n"
"JAVA_HOME=/opt/jdk\n"
"\n"
"# Adjust PATH\n"
"pathappend $JAVA_HOME/bin\n"
"\n"
"# Auto Java CLASSPATH: Copy jar files to, or create symlinks in, the\n"
"# /usr/share/java directory.\n"
"\n"
"AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR=/usr/share/java\n"
"\n"
"pathprepend . CLASSPATH\n"
"\n"
"for dir in `find ${AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR} -type d 2>/dev/null`; do\n"
"    pathappend $dir CLASSPATH\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"for jar in `find ${AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR} -name \"*.jar\" 2>/dev/null`; do\n"
"    pathappend $jar CLASSPATH\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"export JAVA_HOME\n"
"\n"
"# By default, Java creates several files in a directory named\n"
"# /tmp/hsperfdata_[username]. This directory contains files that are used for\n"
"# performance monitoring and profiling, but aren't normally needed on a BLFS\n"
"# system. This environment variable disables that feature.\n"
"_JAVA_OPTIONS=\"-XX:-UsePerfData\"\n"
"\n"
"export _JAVA_OPTIONS\n"
"\n"
"unset AUTO_CLASSPATH_DIR dir jar _JAVA_OPTIONS\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/profile.d/openjdk.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:65
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If <xref linkend=\"sudo\"/> is installed, the super user should have access "
"to the above variables. Execute the following commands as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Se &quot;<xref linkend=\"sudo\"/>&quot; estiver instalado, [então] o(a) "
"superusuário(a) deveria ter acesso às variáveis acima. Execute os seguintes "
"comandos como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:70
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/sudoers.d/java &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>Defaults env_keep += JAVA_HOME\n"
"Defaults env_keep += CLASSPATH\n"
"Defaults env_keep += _JAVA_OPTIONS</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/sudoers.d/java &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>Defaults env_keep += JAVA_HOME\n"
"Defaults env_keep += CLASSPATH\n"
"Defaults env_keep += _JAVA_OPTIONS</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:77
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To use <command>mandb</command> to include the OpenJDK man pages in its "
"database, issue, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root </systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""
"Para usar &quot;<command>mandb</command>&quot; para incluir as páginas de "
"manual do &quot;OpenJDK&quot; na base de dados dele, emita como o(a) "
"usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:82
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/man_db.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin Java addition\n"
"MANDATORY_MANPATH     /opt/jdk/man\n"
"MANPATH_MAP           /opt/jdk/bin     /opt/jdk/man\n"
"MANDB_MAP             /opt/jdk/man     /var/cache/man/jdk\n"
"# End Java addition</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"mkdir -p /var/cache/man &amp;&amp;\n"
"mandb -c /opt/jdk/man</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/man_db.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Inicia adição \"Java\"\n"
"MANDATORY_MANPATH     /opt/jdk/man\n"
"MANPATH_MAP           /opt/jdk/bin     /opt/jdk/man\n"
"MANDB_MAP             /opt/jdk/man     /var/cache/man/jdk\n"
"# Termina Java addition</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"mkdir -p /var/cache/man &amp;&amp;\n"
"mandb -c /opt/jdk/man</userinput>"

#. type: Attribute 'xreflabel' of: <sect1><sect2>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:95
#, xml-text
msgid "installing the JVM Certificate Authority Certificates"
msgstr ""
"instalando os Certificados de Autoridade Certificadora da &quot;JVM&quot;"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:97
#, xml-text
msgid "Setting up the Certificate Authority Certificates for Java"
msgstr "Configurando os Certificados de Autoridade Certificadora para Java"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:100
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>OpenJDK</application> uses its own format for the CA "
"certificates. The Java security modules use "
"<envar>$JAVA_HOME</envar><filename>/lib/security/cacerts</filename> by "
"default. In order to keep all the certificates in one place, we use "
"<filename>/etc/ssl/java/cacerts</filename>. The instructions on the <xref "
"linkend=\"make-ca\"/> page previously created the file located in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/ssl/java</filename>.  Set up a symlink in the "
"default location as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""
"O &quot;<application>OpenJDK</application>&quot; usa o próprio formato dele "
"para os certificados de &quot;AC&quot;. Os módulos de segurança do "
"&quot;Java&quot; usam "
"&quot;<envar>$JAVA_HOME</envar><filename>/lib/security/cacerts</filename>&quot;"
" por padrão. Para a finalidade de manter todos os certificados em um lugar, "
"nós usamos &quot;<filename>/etc/ssl/java/cacerts</filename>&quot;. As "
"instruções na página &quot;<xref linkend=\"make-ca\"/>&quot; criaram "
"anteriormente o arquivo localizado em &quot;<filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/ssl/java</filename>&quot;. Configure um link "
"simbólico no local padrão como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:111
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ln -sfv /etc/pki/tls/java/cacerts "
"/opt/jdk/lib/security/cacerts</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ln -sfv /etc/pki/tls/java/cacerts "
"/opt/jdk/lib/security/cacerts</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:114
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Use the following command to check if the <filename>cacerts</filename> file "
"has been successfully installed:"
msgstr ""
"Use o seguinte comando para verificar se o arquivo "
"&quot;<filename>cacerts</filename>&quot; foi instalado com sucesso:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:118
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>/opt/jdk/bin/keytool -list -cacerts</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>/opt/jdk/bin/keytool -list -cacerts</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:121
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"At the prompt <computeroutput>Enter keystore password:</computeroutput>, "
"enter <userinput>changeit</userinput> (the default) or just press the "
"<quote>Enter</quote> key. If the <filename>cacerts</filename> file was "
"installed correctly, you will see a list of the certificates with related "
"information for each one. If not, you need to reinstall them."
msgstr ""
"No &quot;prompt&quot; &quot;<computeroutput>Enter keystore "
"password:</computeroutput>&quot;, digite "
"&quot;<userinput>changeit</userinput>&quot; (o padrão) ou simplesmente "
"pressione a tecla <quote>Enter</quote>. Se o arquivo "
"&quot;<filename>cacerts</filename>&quot; foi instalado corretamente, [então]"
" você verá uma lista dos certificados com informações relacionadas a cada "
"um. Caso contrário, você precisa reinstalá-los."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/ojdk-conf.xml:129
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you later install a new JVM, you just have to create the symlink in the "
"default location to be able to use the cacerts."
msgstr ""
"Se instalar posteriormente uma nova &quot;JVM&quot;, [então] você apenas tem"
" de criar o link simbólico no local padrão para estar apto(a) a usar o "
"&quot;cacerts&quot;."
